# What the early review of round 1 found, each held by a test.

[break] a-calls-hooks-ignore-an-interrupt
rule: An interrupt, or a response thrown away, while a call's `tool.before` hooks are asked stops them at once.
file: crates/cineris-agent/src/round.rs
in: Planning::hooked
find: self.cx.cancel.race(hooks::ask_all(set, matched, input, self.observers)).await
replace: Some(hooks::ask_all(set, matched, input, self.observers).await)
caught-by:
    cineris-agent::it hooks::an_interrupt_while_a_calls_hooks_are_asked_stops_them
    cineris-agent::it hooks::a_response_thrown_away_while_a_calls_hooks_are_asked_stops_them

[break] the-kept-runs-key-ignores-a-replacement
rule: A run kept from a response thrown away is not used for the same call when a hook replaced its arguments.
file: crates/cineris-agent/src/round.rs
in: Round::planned
find: call.key = format!("{}\u{0}{}\u{0}{}", call.name, call.arguments, replaced.arguments);
replace: let _ = &replaced.arguments;
caught-by:
    cineris-agent::it hooks::a_kept_run_is_not_used_for_a_call_a_hook_replaced

[break] a-replacements-deny-becomes-a-question
rule: A replacement the policy denies stands: it is not put to the user.
